From 76b1c6a3a7dccca6ab78b807973ff8a1a8a14045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:13:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): per-source retention
 (sessions.source_retention_days) [daveey]

Automation transcripts dominate state.db: on tester's MacBook 576k of 985k
messages (and most of the 23 GB file) were Kanban card runs, kept forever
because auto_prune is off to keep chat history.

sessions.source_retention_days ({source: days}) prunes one automation
source's ended sessions past its own window, independent of auto_prune.
Only unattended sources are eligible (SOURCE_RETENTION_SOURCES: cron, kanban,
subagent, tool, recovered); cli/acp/api_server also carry interactive chats
and are refused like desktop/tui. A non-integer or <1 value is skipped with a
warning, so a typo never deletes conversations. Same guards as auto-prune
(pinned and mid-turn rows spared, archived rows included, stale open rows
closed first), its own throttle key, no VACUUM (freed pages are reused, so
the file stops growing).

The CLI start and the gateway housekeeping tick now share
run_sessions_retention(), which reads min_interval_hours only when a feature
that uses it is on (as before) and drops 9 lines from gateway/run.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
